acfa7921e665"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Data source & information:",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0., 0., 1.]],
 "\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/lespin/house-prices-dataset"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8406071850962543`*^9, 3.8406072554331727`*^9}, 
   3.840619410821807*^9},ExpressionUUID->"5541f22e-6062-4e5e-97cb-\
15cd82027cbe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["\nQuestion overview:",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0., 0., 1.]],
 "\nUse Regression (and Gradient Decent) to predict the price of a new house \
that has come on to the market . \nWe have prior data (train.csv) which can \
be found at  https://www.kaggle.com/lespin/house-prices-dataset).\nMake a \
prediction using two different Models : one linear and one non-linear \
(include only one!).\n\n",
 StyleBox["Note: Included in what I am looking for you to show me that you \
understand:\n1. How to use the code I gave you that models a linear function \
and its cost function\n2. How to use the code I gave you to implements \
Gradient Decent on a linear model\n3. How to take the raw data and to turn \
them into suitable features for linear regression\n4. How to split data up so \
that you produce not only a model but an idea of how useful it is.",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 "\n"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8405321901794205`*^9, 3.8405321901808443`*^9}, {
   3.8405322507701707`*^9, 3.8405323569647264`*^9}, {3.8406071234963913`*^9, 
